    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0495" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/242: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-12T09:00:00-03:00">July 12, 1932—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. All ports São Paulo are declared temporarily closed to domestic and foreign
                    shipping by a decree issued last evening.</p>
                <p>The cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Rio Grande do Sul</hi> was despatched last
                    night to Santos which is in the hands of São Paulo forces.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
